WEBVTT

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.370
My heart won't stop pounding.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.160
This is where I've longed to be since that day.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:25.450
To be on stage where only actors can stand.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.790
I'll swallow all my nerves and anxiety.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.370
The bud inside me begins to open.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.620
At this moment, I want to laugh out loud.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.080
I want to shout until my throat is hoarse.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.200
I want to throw all my raw emotions
into my performance.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.620
This is where I belong.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.580
The show must go on.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.870
The bud will go into full bloom!

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.450
Thou seest we are not all alone unhappy.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.200
"15 Complete Works of Shakespeare"
"As You Like It"
Thou seest we are not all alone unhappy.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.830
"15 Complete Works of Shakespeare"
"As You Like It"
--This wide and universal theater

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:20.540
--Look, how cute.
--This wide and universal theater

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.870
--Look, how cute.
--presents more woeful pageants
than the scene wherein we play in.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:27.950
--presents more woeful pageants
than the scene wherein we play in.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:31.250
All the world's a stage,

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:35.580
and all the men and women merely players.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.910
They have their exits and their entrances,

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:43.120
and one man in his time plays many parts.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.580
"2pm Showtime!!"

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.370
"Welcome to Vedulo, City of Theater"

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.620
It was pretty good last time.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:58.700
Yeah, it was.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.160
Tickets for tonight's show still available!

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:10.040
Just say it! I have a
terminal illness, don't I?!

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.370
A street act!

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.700
That's not true!

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.870
Don't lie to me.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:21.200
I saw you and the doctor talking.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.120
Tasuku...

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.620
I don't wanna die not knowing!

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.620
Tell me more about my illness!

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:33.120
We'll attract attention here.
Let's talk at the hospital.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.500
Yeah.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.540
Thanks for watching!

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.580
God Troupe's worth watching!

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.410
Their acting pulls you in!

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:49.200
Excuse me, is God Troupe accepting new members?

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.410
We should be.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:52.830
You've got experience?

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:57.080
Not much. You have dorms there?

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.120
No, we don't.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.500
I see...

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.750
Um...

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.910
If you're looking for a dorm, my troupe's--

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.500
Oh no! Please excuse me!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.290
Please try Mankai Company!

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.620
What was that about?

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.330
Mankai Company?

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:21.540
"Mankai Company"
"Romeo's Heavenly School"

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.160
"Mankai Company"
"Romeo's Heavenly School"
This should be the right place...

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.370
This should be the right place...

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.290
This building looks like it has a <i>long </i>history.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.700
Really...

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.120
"To: Yukio Tachibana"

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.250
"To: Yukio Tachibana"
Dad...

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.330
Hey, you. You've got business at this theater?

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.910
Are you the one who sent the letter-- Whoa!

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.500
Well?!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.120
Dad, you don't owe this guy money, do you?

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.290
It's you...

00:03:55.290 --> 00:04:01.120
Nope, not me! I didn't receive a letter
or anything. I'm just Passerby A!

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.330
Get outta here if you've got no business here.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.790
Unless you like danger.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.620
Danger?

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.370
Oh, yeah! Take a look at my backhoe!

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.660
Nothin's gonna stop this baby!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.120
Boss, can I bust it up?

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.370
Do it, Sakoda.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.830
Please, don't do it!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.750
But just the sign. I'm turning
the building into a bar.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.750
Don't pretend you didn't hear me!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.500
Wh-What are you doing?

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.700
I warned you it'd be dangerous here.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.620
Please, Furuichi! Don't do it!

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:52.160
I said I'd repurpose the place
if you couldn't pay off the debt.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.750
We're about to start a show!

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.450
If we make some money,
I can at least pay off some interest!

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.290
Sakoda, stop.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.290
You're the boss, boss!

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.500
Matsukawa.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.700
Y-Yes?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.540
Presale tickets sold?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.580
Still zero, sir!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.410
Day-of tickets sold?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.250
Zero, sir!

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.790
--When's showtime?
--In three minutes!

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.120
Sakoda, you've got this.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:24.160
Wait, please! It's our new member's debut show!

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.080
What?

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.080
No actor would ever forget their debut show!

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:32.000
How sad would it be to tear down
the theater right before their debut show!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.870
--You have zero audience. You call that a show?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:36.040
--I-I'll be...
--You have zero audience. You call that a show?

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.700
...w-watching the show!

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:53.290
Better not regret stopping by to watch.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:30.250
Hey! I'm Romeo Kadota!
First year in high school!

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:34.120
I have a crush on a girl in my class!

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:38.700
Oh no! It's so late! I've gotta to go to school!

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.500
He's the new member, huh.
And the other troupe members--

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.910
Hey, wait up, Romeo.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.160
Take me with ya.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.790
It's a parrot?!

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.580
All right! I'm gonna go see her!

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:02.500
A fall like this is nothing
compared to this joy!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:08.790
Aw, how come she won't like me back?

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:15.540
Nothing discourages him. Looks like
he's so happy just to be on stage.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:21.450
I-I'm going to the ballgame at the castle!

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.000
To the <i>ball</i>!

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:30.330
My first play was also so fun.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.500
I was so immersed...

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.120
...it ended before I knew it.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.120
Thank you very much!

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:51.750
Now that's over.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.000
Demolition time.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:02.160
What?! Even after watching
how hard he worked?! You monster!

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.290
How hard he worked?

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:06.410
Yeah! He got his feelings across!

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:11.830
You think this is a school play where
kids show off how hard they've worked?

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:16.370
This is a place where professionals
are paid to entertain.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:20.040
You're not wrong... Someday, if he works hard--

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:23.950
In this world, just working hard
doesn't do the damn trick!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:30.080
You won't get anywhere with just hard work.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:34.080
You have no talent for acting.

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:41.080
End of discussion. This troupe's
going to be shut down.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.120
Wait, please!

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.750
Um... We really won't have this place anymore?

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.700
Yeah.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.750
I just joined yesterday!

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:55.910
I'm still no good at acting, but I love theater!

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:59.040
Please don't tear this place down!

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.540
Tough luck.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:06.580
No way...

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:24.660
The show must go on.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:31.370
Please, wait!

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:36.000
I beg you! I need this place!

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.580
I've already decided.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.330
I won't let you!

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.450
Manager...

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:44.250
I have to protect this place at all costs!

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.750
Matsukawa, I've given you
more than enough chances.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:48.580
But--

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:51.000
There's no more room for negotiation.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.330
There's still a possibility
things will turn upward...

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.370
Not a chance.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:07.080
If only Yukio returned
to make it like the old days.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.950
By Yukio...

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:17.790
...you mean my dad, Yukio Tachibana?

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:21.200
Are you Yukio's daughter?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.700
"From: Isuke Matsukawa"

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.910
That's the letter I sent! Where's Yukio?

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:32.040
I haven't heard from him for eight years.
He hasn't come home, either.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.160
I see...

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:37.500
Not what you expected? It's over.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:42.620
How rude! There might be another way!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:47.500
You can only say that because you
know nothing about this theater.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.250
Believe it or not, this theater is
exclusively for the troupe.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:56.580
"Under Construction"
Most troupes rent venues for
their shows, but not this troupe.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.000
"Under Construction"
Along with the costs of maintaining its dorm,

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.120
"Under Construction"
the funds needed to upkeep this place is steep.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.790
In its heyday until eight years ago,
this troupe brought in revenue by having

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:10.750
four sub-troupes--Spring, Summer,
Autumn, and Winter--perform year-round.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:17.200
This troupe can't stay afloat unless it
has four groups performing constantly.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:23.790
But all we have here is a brat
who only joined yesterday.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.200
--Sakoda.
--Wha-- Sir?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.290
Do it.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.250
I-I just remembered!

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:45.540
What did you remember?

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:51.910
T-Truth is, my dad left the troupe to me
if anything happened to him.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.500
Really?

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.080
We just have to get four sub-troupes, right?

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:57.410
Well, yes.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:02.500
That'll be easy! I'll bring in
some more troupe members!

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.950
How many?

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:07.080
Er... I can get two more right away!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:13.500
You have until sunset.
I'll wait until sunset today.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.750
Bring two new members to me.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.540
If you can't, don't hope to see
that theater sign again.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:23.540
I understand! Let's go, you two.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:25.500
--Yes, ma'am!
--You're the boss, boss!

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:30.950
Crappy acting.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:33.910
Nothing like Yukio.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:39.620
What?! You were lying earlier?!

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:42.250
Not exactly lying... I was acting!

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:44.330
So when you said you have new members...

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.250
I don't have any.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.370
I can't believe it!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.870
So we're going to be shut down?

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:53.040
We have to find new members to prevent that!

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.700
It's way too late for that!

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:58.290
You never know until you try!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.910
Nope! Impossible!

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:04.830
Everybody left and only
one person's joined since...

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.410
--...and it's not like I'm
popular or anything...

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.500
--It's going to work out!
--...and it's not like I'm
popular or anything...

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.200
I don't know what I can do, but I want to help!

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:15.250
I don't want to lose the troupe I just joined.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:20.580
I never introduced myself.
I'm Izumi Tachibana. Nice to meet you.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:26.000
I'm Sakuya Sakuma. "Saku" as in
a blooming flower. Nice to meet you, ma'am!

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.700
Come on, Manager. Get a grip on yourself.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.790
Fine. There's not a chance,
but I guess we should try.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:39.580
I've got an idea for how to get people quick.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:44.500
Hey, everyone! I'm Mankai Company's manager!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:47.200
We're about to hold a street audition!

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:50.700
Here! I'm up first! Sakuya Sakuma, 17 years old!

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.160
My talent is remembering
peoples faces and names!

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.290
--Is that a street act?
--My hobby is rehearsing lines near the river!

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.410
--He's so loud.
--My hobby is rehearsing lines near the river!

00:13:57.410 --> 00:14:00.500
Just as planned, we're getting attention.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:04.870
Director! What's the first question
for the audition?

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.330
You're asking <i>me</i>?

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:14.870
Uh... Right, the first question will be...
I mean... here's the question!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.830
I can't watch. Think they lost a bet?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.120
Maybe it's part of their act.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.370
You serious?!

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:21.950
Go on, Director!

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:26.160
R-Right! First question:

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:29.450
Wh-What are your strengths?

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:34.500
No one's giving us a second glance.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:44.950
Are you interested in theater?

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.330
Is that Masumi?

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.080
You know him, Sakuya?

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:52.830
He's in the grade below me at school.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:54.500
Who're you?

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.330
I guess he doesn't recognize me.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:02.700
Er... Masumi, if you're interested in theater,
why not join the troupe?

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.830
You're part of the troupe?

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:07.200
Huh? I'm not...

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.700
You're not?

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:13.450
Don't be shy, Director. You're our
supervisor and general director!

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:17.540
What?! I just said that for the street act--

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.250
--I'll join if you're in.
--What?!

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:27.660
Masumi, you're joining?

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.200
I don't care about you.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.450
--N-No matter. I'm so happy!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.080
--I didn't plan to actually join the troupe...
--N-No matter. I'm so happy!

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.750
Ow-ow-ouch!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.250
Well, we have a new member.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:44.040
Member number two, Masumi Usui, 16 years old.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.580
My hobby is listening to music, I guess.

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:51.080
I joined the troupe to do
my best for our director.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.330
Masumi's amazing!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:16:00.160
He's competent and has flair.
It's hard to believe this is his first time--

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.790
--Director.
--Whoa!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.330
Was that okay?

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:04.410
Y-Yeah.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:05.580
How was I?

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.370
Your acting was very g--

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:09.500
Not asking you.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.580
I-It was good. Keep going.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.620
He's a strange kid.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:20.950
How about this?

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.700
Quit asking every second!

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:29.160
I guess time's up.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:32.000
Just one more! Is there anyone...

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:35.330
It's him!

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:36.870
Sakuya?

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.620
He was asking around for a troupe
with a dorm earlier today!

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:41.080
Really?

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:44.160
I have a knack for remembering faces!

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.540
Let's go!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.040
I go where you go.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.580
Wait!

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:01.450
Please! Wait!

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:14.620
All the world's a stage,

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:18.370
and all the men and women merely players.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.790
--They have their exits and their entrances,

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.450
--Huh? These lines...
--They have their exits and their entrances,

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.120
--Huh? These lines...
--and one man in his time plays many parts,

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:24.870
--Where are they from?
--and one man in his time plays many parts,

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.750
--and one man in his time plays many parts,

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:28.870
--his acts being seven ages.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:30.830
--Shakespeare?
--his acts being seven ages.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.000
--his acts being seven ages.

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:36.870
At first the infant,

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:40.700
mewling and puking in the nurse's arms.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:44.620
And then the whining school-boy.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:50.870
With his satchel and shining morning face,

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:55.410
creeping like snail unwillingly to school.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.950
And then the lover,

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:06.790
sighing like furnace, with a woeful ballad
made to his mistress' eyebrow.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:14.450
Then a soldier, full of strange oaths,
and bearded like the pard.

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:19.040
Jealous in honor, sudden,
and quick in quarrel...

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.290
Excuse me.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:24.750
Are you interested in
joining a theater troupe?

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.700
We have the dorm you're looking for, too.

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:30.790
How'd you know that?

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:34.160
I have no theater experience. That okay?

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:36.660
I joined without any.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:42.160
I'd actually rather write plays
than be an actor.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:45.750
Then you can be an actor
<i>and </i>playwright. How's that?

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:48.290
Sign me up!

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.500
Yippee!

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.290
I'm Tsuzuru Minagi.

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:55.040
Nice to meet you, Tsuzuru.

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.910
Even I could write a script.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:58.450
It's not a competition!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.080
We've got to get back fast, ma'am!

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:06.290
I'll explain everything later!
Anyway, let's hustle!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.830
Seems there's a good reason behind it.

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:21.870
So you didn't turn tail and run off.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.160
We made it... right?

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:28.790
Got in just under the wire.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:31.290
You won't demolish the place, then?

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:37.200
Can't breathe easy yet. It just means that
I won't be demolishing the sign today.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:38.160
What?!

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.370
We're disbanding?

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:41.950
This guy's brutal.

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:45.750
And here I thought we could finally
start up a new Spring Troupe.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.200
A new Spring Troupe?

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.450
Yes! And have a debut show
once we gather enough members!

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.540
When is that?

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:56.540
Huh? Er... When do you think, Director?

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:57.410
You're asking <i>me</i>?!

00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:58.830
Director!

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:06.500
Let's see... We'd have to start from the basics
and rehearse, so maybe six months--

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:07.330
Next month.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:08.410
What?

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.500
Rehearse your butts off and
put on a show sometime next month.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:14.950
That's impossible!

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:18.200
Listen here, this is your last chance.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:23.330
If you can fulfill the following three
conditions, I'll extend the debt deadline.

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:25.000
What conditions?

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:29.790
One: The new Spring Troupe is to launch
their debut show within the next month

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.790
with a full house on closing night.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:36.910
Two: Form four sub-troupes
by the end of the year

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:39.660
with each troupe running successful shows.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:44.500
Three: The debt is to be
fully paid off within one year.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:49.540
If even one condition is not fulfilled,
I will demolish the place, no questions asked.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.120
Within the year? That's ridicu--

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:55.410
Quit whining! You know
how much debt the troupe's in?!

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:56.700
Ten million yen!

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:58.000
Dang!

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:01.790
You hear me? This is as far as I'll compromise.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:09.700
Unless you plan to shoulder the debt?
Then that's a different discussion.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.040
Get your hands off her!

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:17.410
And one last thing.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:18.700
What is it?

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:24.410
You will be this troupe's general director.
That's the last condition.

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:26.160
Wh-Why me?

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:31.790
I see. So you <i>are </i>going to run away.
Just like your father.

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.700
What are you getting at?

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:40.370
I heard your father was the general director,
yet he abandoned the troupe.

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:45.120
He must've bailed out when he realized
he couldn't keep this place afloat.

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:49.120
Yukio would never do that!
He truly loved theater!

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:52.080
Loving something doesn't mean you're fit for it.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:57.790
So that's the story.
You all better bear that in mind.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.120
Even so...

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:09.950
...there are so many things you can
work hard at because you love it!

00:22:14.290 --> 00:22:19.450
And if that doesn't work out, you just need to
keep on working harder and harder!

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:25.910
I love the stage. So I'll never run away,
no matter how hard things get!

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:33.910
As for me, I'm not gonna run
before I even start.

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:39.290
I haven't done anything for the director yet.

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:52.080
Okay.

00:22:53.950 --> 00:22:57.160
I'll be this troupe's general director.

00:23:05.870 --> 00:23:07.080
"To a Future in Full Bloom"
Yes, ma'am!

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:08.290
"To a Future in Full Bloom"
